# VTID-03958 — commands run during this change

## Investigation

Read the full AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml end to end (Read tool, whole file,
907 lines) before touching anything, and confirmed the ceiling situation the
task described was accurate:

$ python3 -c "
import yaml
doc = yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml'))
inputs = doc['on']['workflow_dispatch']['inputs'] if 'on' in doc else doc[True]['workflow_dispatch']['inputs']
print('count:', len(inputs))
"
  count: 25   # exactly at GitHub's hard ceiling, confirmed before any edit

Studied the "Build task-definition (2/2 — optional overrides) + register +
roll the service" step's existing per-flag pattern (nova_sonic_global_enabled,
dev_autopilot_executor_enabled blocks) as the upsert idiom to follow:
  env: NAME_INPUT: ${{ inputs.name }}
  if [ -n "$NAME_INPUT" ]; then
    NEW_DEF=$(echo "$NEW_DEF" | jq --arg V "$NAME_INPUT" '
      .containerDefinitions[0].environment |=
        ( [ .[] | select(.name != "ENV_VAR_NAME") ] + [ {name:"ENV_VAR_NAME", value:$V} ] )')
  fi

Read the guard test first:
$ cat services/gateway/test/scripts/workflow-dispatch-input-limit.test.ts
  Confirmed it parses every *.yml in .github/workflows with js-yaml, extracts
  on.workflow_dispatch.inputs, and fails if any file has >25. Also has a
  "near the ceiling" warning-only check (>=23) and two sanity checks (some
  files get counted; AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml specifically stays <=25).
  Confirmed it does NOT hardcode 25 permanently for this file at a lower
  number, so a 24-input result after this change passes cleanly.

