## Fix

.github/workflows/AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml:
  1. Removed the `nova_canary_user_ids` / `nova_canary_tenant_ids`
     workflow_dispatch inputs (2 inputs removed).
  2. Removed `NOVA_USERS_INPUT` / `NOVA_TENANTS_INPUT` env wiring on the
     "Build task-definition (2/2)" step, and removed the
     NOVA_SONIC_CANARY_USER_IDS / NOVA_SONIC_CANARY_TENANT_IDS upsert from
     inside the nova_sonic_enabled override block (that block now only
     touches NOVA_SONIC_ENABLED / NOVA_SONIC_REGION / NOVA_SONIC_MODEL_ID).
  3. Added ONE new `env_overrides` workflow_dispatch input (JSON object
     string; EMPTY = no-op) — 1 input added. Net: 25 -> 24.
  4. Wired `ENV_OVERRIDES_INPUT: ${{ inputs.env_overrides }}` on the same
     step's `env:` block.
  5. Added a new override block at the END of the optional-overrides chain
     (after every named-input block, so it can override anything they set):
       - validates env_overrides is well-formed JSON via `jq -e . >/dev/null`
         and fails the step loudly (::error::, exit 1) if not
       - validates it is a JSON OBJECT (not an array/string/number) and
         fails loudly if not
       - generically upserts every key via `to_entries` (no hardcoded key
         names — works for OPERATOR_EXECUTION_ONRAMP_ENABLED today and any
         future flag with zero further code change)
       - logs the applied key list, matching every other block's log-line
         convention
  6. Updated the file's header comment (the block describing the original
     26-input parse-failure incident) to note env_overrides now exists as
     the escape hatch, and where it lives in this file.
  7. Deliberately did NOT put the literal string "OPERATOR_EXECUTION_ONRAMP_ENABLED"
     anywhere in this file's text (see "Test conflict found and resolved"
     below) — the description uses a generic {"SOME_ENV_VAR":"value"}
     example instead.

## Test conflict found and resolved (worth recording)

First draft used the task's own suggested example
`{"OPERATOR_EXECUTION_ONRAMP_ENABLED":"true", ...}` verbatim inside the new
input's `description:` field. Running the existing test suite surfaced a
real, intentional regression guard this tripped:

$ cd services/gateway && npx jest test/vtid-03820-onramp-staging-flag-pinned.test.ts --silent
  FAIL — "is deliberately NOT pinned on the prod deploy workflow yet"
  expect(prodYml).not.toContain('OPERATOR_EXECUTION_ONRAMP_ENABLED')

That test (VTID-03820) exists specifically so that promoting the on-ramp
flag to prod stays a deliberate, later, separately-reviewed decision, not a
silent byproduct of an unrelated change landing text in this file. Per this
session's instruction to never weaken a guard test, reworded the
env_overrides description/comments to use a generic placeholder
(`{"SOME_ENV_VAR":"value"}`) instead of the literal flag name. This does
NOT reduce the actual capability being built — the mechanism still lets an
operator apply `OPERATOR_EXECUTION_ONRAMP_ENABLED=true` (or anything else)
at DISPATCH time via `-f env_overrides='{"OPERATOR_EXECUTION_ONRAMP_ENABLED":"true"}'`,
which never adds that string to this file at all, so VTID-03820's guard
stays meaningful and green, and the actual promotion of that specific flag
to prod remains the separate, deliberate, later action its own test says
it should be. Re-ran after the fix — all green (see below).

## New tests

services/gateway/test/vtid-03958-env-overrides-input.test.ts (15 tests):
  - the two retired inputs are gone; env_overrides exists; net count is 24
  - the nova_sonic_enabled override block no longer references the removed
    env wiring
  - ENV_OVERRIDES_INPUT is wired from inputs.env_overrides
  - extracts the REAL env_overrides jq block from the workflow file (not a
    reimplementation) and executes it with the real `jq` binary against
    sample task-definition JSON:
      - EMPTY input is a true no-op (byte-for-byte passthrough)
      - adds a brand-new key generically
      - upserts (replaces) an existing key, exactly one survives
      - applies multiple keys in one call (to_entries, no fixed arity)
      - coerces a non-string JSON value (bool/number) to a string
      - malformed JSON fails loudly (non-zero exit, ::error::, never a
        silent no-op)
      - non-object JSON (array/string) fails loudly
      - a validation failure never reaches (or prints) a mutated NEW_DEF

